# direnv: auto-enter the pinned toolchain, so the tools you get are the
# tools CI gets. The flake sits at the repo ROOT, which is what lets it see
# `Cargo.toml`/`src/` and offer a real package -- a flake in a subdirectory
# has its own directory as its source root and can offer none.
#
# Entering also puts `nanokit` itself on PATH via a `cargo run` shim, so the
# tool can format and check its own spec (V24) without anyone typing a cargo
# invocation, and installs the git hooks (V23).
use flake
